{{also|Boxen}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɒksən|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|boxen|lang=enm}}, replacing earlier {{term|bixen|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|byxen||made of boxwood|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{suffix|box|en|lang=en}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# Made of [[boxwood]].
# Resembling [[box]] (the wood).

===Etymology 2===
A nonstandard plural of {{term|box|lang=en}} formed by analogy with {{term|oxen|lang=en}}. The standard plural of ''box'' is {{term|boxes|lang=en}}; ''-en'' is no longer a plural in standard use. See ''[[-en#Etymology 2|-en]]'' for details.

====Noun====
{{head|en|noun plural form}}

# {{plural of|box||computer|lang=en}}

